cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Sabot — the specification, the harness, or published Sabot Score results — please cite it as below."
title: "Sabot: an own-checks fault-detection standard for multi-agent frameworks"
authors:
  - family-names: Otterson
    given-names: Jeff
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jott2121/sabot"
url: "https://github.com/Jott2121/sabot"
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: v0.2.0
date-released: "2026-07-24"
abstract: "Sabot plants controlled faults inside running multi-agent pipelines and scores what fraction the pipeline's own checks catch. Wave 1 (900 faults; LangGraph, CrewAI, AutoGen/Magentic-One) measured a median hard-tier detection rate of 16.7%, with recovery-without-detection the dominant outcome in every row. Wave 2 (825 paired faults) measured a pre-registered anomaly-first reporting protocol that raised the median to 55.0%, while showing that reporting is not reacting. Both preprints, the frozen specification, the harness, and the full raw-trace corpus are published here."
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - fault injection
  - agent evaluation
  - guardrails
  - benchmark
